/* A course is not deleted with the public key (round AW, lead's own fix, run any time). The policy courses_creator_delete lets a signed in creator delete a whole course row straight through the public API, and ON DELETE CASCADE then takes its modules, its lessons, their attachments and every buyer's lesson progress (course_progress) with it, past the app's own rules: Storelib never deletes a sold course (a product anybody bought is archived, app/api/products/delete), and a community program with buyers is refused ("Move it to draft instead", lib/communities/server/learn.ts). Every course delete the app makes runs on the server key (lib/courses/manage.ts and lib/communities/server/learn.ts, both through the service role), so DELETE and TRUNCATE on public.courses are taken from anon and authenticated, as part 452 did for products and stores. Deleting a single module or lesson in the course builder is unchanged (course_modules and course_lessons keep their policies). The server key, and its cascades, still delete. It does NOT change or read any row. A missing table is skipped with a notice. Safe to run again. */
DO $do$ BEGIN IF to_regclass('public.courses') IS NULL THEN RAISE NOTICE 'part 461: public.courses does not exist here, skipped'; RETURN; END IF; EXECUTE 'REVOKE DELETE, TRUNCATE ON public.courses FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated'; END $do$;
notify pgrst, 'reload schema';
